# Re-apply the power policy when the AC line changes.
#
# The kernel emits a power_supply "change" uevent on both the Mains supply and
# the battery when the charger is plugged or pulled. Only the Mains one is
# matched: the battery emits a change event on every capacity tick, which
# would restart the unit every few seconds for no reason.
#
# `systemctl start --no-block` and not RUN+= with the script directly: udev
# kills anything still running in a RUN+= after a short timeout, and the
# script writes several hundred sysfs files across the PCI bus.
SUBSYSTEM=="power_supply", ACTION=="change", ATTR{type}=="Mains", \
    RUN+="/usr/bin/systemctl start --no-block myosi-power-tune.service"
